{"id": "60c7be6b52f29dc802823b25d91f8a25", "text": "verse clarifies that one cannot expect to acquire direct knowledge \n(aparoksha ) immedi ately after acquiring indirect knowledge. One must \nrepeatedly study scriptures with the mind fully immersed in the Lord and  \nensure that the knowledge acquired is without any doubts and develop full \nconviction in such knowledge. This will allow a seeker to be prepared to \nabsorb direct, divine, spiritual knowledge which leads the seeker to \nmoksha . \n \nThe Learned See the Lord in All", "embedding": [0.027037419378757477, 0.043301865458488464, 0.01231718435883522, 0.006538561079651117, -0.025346405804157257, -0.05353515222668648, 0.14058342576026917, -0.020599856972694397, 0.06192362308502197, 0.03801051527261734, 0.04403362795710564, 0.012417296878993511, 0.07745499908924103, -0.026441941037774086, 0.004060213454067707, 0.043631523847579956, -0.038900405168533325, -0.023101478815078735, -0.021690377965569496, -0.08469580113887787, 0.022523600608110428, 0.05700055509805679, 0.002419585594907403, -0.027714209631085396, -0.06349541991949081, -0.005775996018201113, -0.028129570186138153, -0.03480822592973709, 0.0922127440571785, -0.026533715426921844, 0.04969210550189018, 0.010075532831251621, -0.028185540810227394, 0.018928201869130135, -0.06899038702249527, 0.1432870477437973, 0.011544730514287949, 0.06268632411956787, -0.002600474748760462, -0.0038471880834549665, 0.020507218316197395, 0.013522705994546413, -0.05562765151262283, -0.04892776533961296, 0.10503777116537094, -0.05878760293126106, -0.04460155591368675, 0.00793963298201561, 0.037990912795066833, -0.035971783101558685, -0.16812224686145782, -0.09708759188652039, -0.0404147244989872, 0.01846235804259777, -0.026018690317869186, 0.02272857539355755, -0.07630965858697891, 0.097008615732193, -0.010859159752726555, -0.043139152228832245, -0.03817262500524521, -0.026052096858620644, 0.020375335589051247, 0.01244908943772316, 0.029412589967250824, -0.0937474220991134